  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\n\nCooler temperatures arrive behind the front Sunday and Monday with \nhighs in the 70s and 80s. High pressure moves in for those days\ntoo which should help keep us mostly dry until late Monday when\nmore rain chances arrive (30-50% in northeast Nebraska) as \nanother H5 wave approaches the area. Continued waves \napproaching from the northwest will lead to continued storm \nchances through the rest of the extended period. Tuesday night \ninto Wednesday appears to be the best chance areawide (50-70%) \nas a more powerful wave rides the northwesterly flow into the \narea. These storms could be strong to severe as highlighted by \nthe various machine learning algorithms. Highs cool to the 70s \nand 80s by Wednesday and Thursday.",
